079 0 obj<</A 24246 0 R/Alt(Two-panel 3D plot showing a robotic arm interacting with green blocks and spheres. The left panel depicts the arm positioned over a block with labeled axes A, B, and C. The right panel shows the arm in a different orientation, interacting with a cluster o\f spheres on the block. The scene is set on a grid background, emphasizing spatial relationships.)/K 2/P 24038 0 R/Pg 254 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj24080 0 obj<</K 3/P 24038 0 R/Pg 254 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj24081 0 obj<</K[5 24238 0 R 24239 0 R 8 24240 0 R 10 24241 0 R 12]/P 24038 0 R/Pg 254 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj24082 0 obj<</K 3/P 24038 0 R/Pg 259 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj24083 0 obj<</K[4 24236 0 R 6]/P 24038 0 R/Pg 259 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj24084 0 obj<</K[7 24230 0 R 9 24231 0 R 11 24232 0 R 13]/P 24038 0 R/Pg 259 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj24085 0 obj<</A 24229 0 R/Alt(Flow chart illustrating a system for reactive trajectory planning. The chart is divided into two sections: "SSM" and "Reactive Trajectory Planning." In the SSM section, components like "gazebo," "/arm_controller," "/gripper_controller," and "/joint_states\" connect to "move_group," which also links to "speed_adaption," "rviz," and "environment_subscriber." The "move_group" connects to "/planning_scene." The "parameter_loader" and "robot_state_publisher" feed into "/tf." In the Reactive Trajectory Planning \section, "/execute_trajectory" connects to "trajectory_executor," "/ready," and "/stage_name," which link to "execution_controller." "human_publisher" and "collision_checker" connect to "/interrupt_movement." Arrows indicate data flow between components.)/K 14/P 24038 0 R/Pg 259 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj24086 0 obj<</K 15/P 24038 0 R/Pg 259 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj24087 0 obj<</K 1/P 24038 0 R/Pg 262 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj24088 0 obj<</K 2/P 24038 0 R/Pg 262 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj24089 0 